| `dependency_audit.max_review_days` | integer | `90` | a whole number, 1 or more | `scripts/audit_dependencies.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `dependency_audit.max_review_days` row | Sets the most days after the run's date, as `scripts/run_date.py` `today` reads it, an accepted row's `review_by` may be: a row set further out fails `make fe-audit` as parked, naming the row, its date and this key, so an acceptance is renewed rather than parked; a date exactly this many days out passes. Another value is refused with exit 14. Absent, the audit writes `[using default] dependency_audit.max_review_days = 90` to stderr. | the expiry itself: `dependency_audit.accepted.<app>.<advisory>.review_by` | always |
